<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      Weekends inside the neighbouring month get their own fill (DESIGN §5).

      What was there. The cell fill priority puts "other month" above "weekend", so
      inside the neighbouring month's block Sat/Sun were painted exactly like weekdays: the weekend column
      broke off at the month boundary. In 0300 this was recorded as an accepted consequence, but
      the consequence turned out costlier than thought: at the start of a month the neighbouring month takes
      most of the window (measured 02.08.2026: 19 cells out of 28), i.e. weekends are invisible
      on two thirds of the calendar.

      Why this does NOT repeat the 0290 mistake. There the whole other-month block darkened at once;
      here only its Sat/Sun darken: at most 2 cells out of 7, with 19 other-month cells that is
      5-6 cells. A mass darkening does not happen by construction.

      The step down from cal-othermonth is about 4.7 L*, larger than the "weekend above a future
      day" step. It cannot be smaller: the figure in the other month is dimmed already (text-secondary), and
      a quiet step on a dimmed cell does not read.
    -->
    <!--
      Along the way the weekend itself is lowered by another ~2 L*. Above a FUTURE day (bg-surface-muted) it
      rose by only 1.6 L*, and the window is half future: in the future half
      the Sat/Sun column did not read at all (measured on the live board 02.08.2026: a future weekday
      rgb(243,230,222) against a future weekend rgb(240,225,216)). The 0290 edit only assigned this difference
      but did not make it visible.

      A side effect accepted deliberately: a weekend becomes slightly DARKER than a weekday of
      the neighbouring month. They are not confused: the other month has a second mark, the dimmed figure.
    -->
    <changeSet id="0310-wave-01-weekend-deeper" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme SET tokens = tokens || $J${"cal-weekend": "#ecdbd0"}$J$::jsonb WHERE key = 'wave-01';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme SET tokens = tokens || $J${"cal-weekend": "#f0e1d8"}$J$::jsonb WHERE key = 'wave-01';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="0310-wave-02-weekend-deeper" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme SET tokens = tokens || $J${"cal-weekend": "#cce2f8"}$J$::jsonb WHERE key = 'wave-02';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme SET tokens = tokens || $J${"cal-weekend": "#d8ebfd"}$J$::jsonb WHERE key = 'wave-02';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="0310-wave-01-othermonth-weekend" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme SET tokens = tokens || $J${"cal-othermonth-weekend": "#e3d2c5"}$J$::jsonb WHERE key = 'wave-01';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme SET tokens = tokens - 'cal-othermonth-weekend' WHERE key = 'wave-01';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- Wave 02: the same ladder in its blue tones. -->
    <changeSet id="0310-wave-02-othermonth-weekend" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme SET tokens = tokens || $J${"cal-othermonth-weekend": "#bed6ed"}$J$::jsonb WHERE key = 'wave-02';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme SET tokens = tokens - 'cal-othermonth-weekend' WHERE key = 'wave-02';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
